inline_default_outside_datasource: in an ordinary .ssl script the inline
`:PARAMETERS p := v` form does not compile. Each inline default reports
an error from the name through `:=`, at script level and in a procedure
signature.
-- input.ssl --
:PARAMETERS sFleet := "F1", nLimit := 5;
:PROCEDURE CountTrucks;
	:PARAMETERS sCode, nMax := 10;
	:RETURN Len(sCode) + nMax;
:ENDPROC;
:RETURN DoProc("CountTrucks", {sFleet, nLimit});
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sFleet := "F1", nLimit := 5;

:PROCEDURE CountTrucks;
	:PARAMETERS sCode, nMax := 10;

	:RETURN Len(sCode) + nMax;
:ENDPROC;

:RETURN DoProc("CountTrucks", {sFleet, nLimit});
-- diagnostics --
1:13-1:22 error inline_default_outside_datasource: Inline ':=' defaults on ':PARAMETERS' are valid only in data source files; move the default for 'sFleet' to a ':DEFAULT' line after ':PARAMETERS'
1:29-1:38 error inline_default_outside_datasource: Inline ':=' defaults on ':PARAMETERS' are valid only in data source files; move the default for 'nLimit' to a ':DEFAULT' line after ':PARAMETERS'
3:21-3:28 error inline_default_outside_datasource: Inline ':=' defaults on ':PARAMETERS' are valid only in data source files; move the default for 'nMax' to a ':DEFAULT' line after ':PARAMETERS'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
